      "message": "Yeah - I would think so. If we remove the foreign key constraint momentarily we have a small slice of time where it\u0027s possible to do things on the federated_table and protocol_table without the constraint being enforced, since we\u0027re not making the tables read only either.\n\nDo we have the ability to do the following with triggers? \n\n- create a new foreign key constraint using a specific name (expand phase)\n- drop the old foreign key constraint (contract phase)\n- rename the new constraint (contract phase)",
